            0.043
          ],
          "content": "Chapter 6 — Pressure, Winds, Storms, and Cyclones"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.892,
            0.03,
            0.917,
            0.045
          ],
          "content": "85"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.083,
            0.744,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": "You observe water flowing out through the holes on the sides of the bottle. What can you infer from this observation? It **indicates** that water also exerts pressure on the sides of a container. Therefore, we can conclude that liquids exert pressure not only at the bottom of the container, but also on its sides. In fact liquids exert pressure in all directions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.196,
            0.744,
            0.272
          ],
          "content": "You must have seen water spurting out like a fountain from leaking joints or holes in water pipes. Can you explain why this happens? Is it due to the pressure exerted by water on the walls of the pipes?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.283,
            0.345,
            0.305
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ever heard of ..."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.315,
            0.42,
            0.501
          ],
          "content": "Do you know that the base of a dam is much broader than the top? This is because a broad base not only supports the structure of the dam, but also withstands the horizontal water pressure near the bottom (Fig. 6.8). The water stored in the dam, exerts pressure horizontally on the side walls of the dam and vertically on"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.421,
            0.317,
            0.734,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.551,
                0.486,
                0.663,
                0.5
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 6.8: Dam"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.501,
            0.753,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "the floor due to the height of the water level. The pressure which acts horizontally, is very large near its bottom. Thus, to withstand the pressure, the base of the dam is made broader."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.763,
            0.46,
            0.852,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_5_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.569,
            0.658,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": "Let us now try to understand if air also exerts pressure."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.604,
            0.506,
            0.627
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "6.2 Pressure Exerted by Air"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.64,
            0.744,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": "You already know that air is all around us. The envelope of air surrounding the Earth is called **atmosphere**. The atmospheric air contains nitrogen, oxygen, argon, carbon dioxide, and other gases in small quantities. The atmosphere extends up to many kilometres above the surface of the Earth."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.735,
            0.743,
            0.774
          ],
          "content": "Let us find out if the atmosphere exerts pressure by performing the following activity."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.785,
            0.482,
            0.809
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 6.3: Let us explore"
        },
        {
